     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered it. I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily on a confirmation alone, without a clinical reason.\n\nThere's no established use of amlodipine above 10 mg a day. At 50 mg, the patient faces a real risk of severe hypotension, shock and a long-lasting overdose. Your \"Yes, I confirm\" might also have been meant for my question about a typo rather than for the 50 mg dose. With a mistake this serious, I need to be sure before going ahead.\n\nHere's how we can proceed:\n\n1. **If you meant 5 mg or 10 mg**, tell me which and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **If 50 mg is intended**, give me the clinical reason (for example, a protocol or specialist recommendation). I'll enter the order with that reason in the note so a pharmacist can review it before it's given.\n3. **If you don't want to go through me**, you can enter the order directly in the order-entry system or call pharmacy. Either way, a pharmacist will review the dose.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
      }
